<title>GERMANY: German opposition SPD wants EMU to start on time.</title>
<headline>German opposition SPD wants EMU to start on time.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's opposition Social Democrats (SPD) want European monetary union (EMU) to start on time on January 1, 1999, with strict application of the stability criteria, the party said in a statement following a presidium meeting on Monday.</p>
<p>It said EMU is a historic chance for Europe. &quot;This chance must not be missed due to the dilettantish economic and fiscal policies of the Kohl government,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-</p>
